  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Preliminary 0.4.0 release. BREAKING: ISequentialFile gains CompleteAsync, and a streamed write is published only when it completes; the Parquet, ORC and Lance writers publish only on CloseAsync/FinishAsync, and disposing one without closing abandons the file. ITableFileSystem gains PathConstraints, which every implementation must provide. IStatisticsAccessor and INanCountAccessor (and ParquetStatisticsAccessor) take a column path (a list of name parts) instead of a dotted name. SetPredicate.Values holds expressions rather than LiteralValues. LiteralValue equality is now type-exact: LiteralValue.Of(1) no longer equals LiteralValue.Of(1L). IsolationLevel moves from EngineeredWood.DeltaLake.Table to EngineeredWood.DeltaLake. DeltaConflictException.AttemptedVersion is long? (null replaces -1), and ColumnStats.NumRecords is long?. DeletionVectorReader.ReadAsync returns, and DeletionVectorWriter.CreateAsync takes, a DeletionVectorBitmap instead of a set of longs. DeltaPath.EscapePathName takes the partition path spelling and the target storage's PathNameConstraints. IcebergCompat.NestedFieldIdsKey is removed. Many methods gained optional parameters (CommitProperties, overwrite flags, writer options), so code compiled against 0.3.0 must be recompiled. FSST (experimental) is written as Parquet encoding 12. New in Delta Lake: DELETE, UPDATE and MERGE (deletion vectors or copy-on-write), RESTORE, replaceWhere, mergeSchema, ADD/DROP CONSTRAINT, CHECK constraints and generated columns evaluated with Spark semantics, IcebergCompatV3, DeltaTransaction for multi-operation commits, and scan filters pushed down to Parquet row groups and pages. New in Parquet: page indexes written and used for pruning by default, dictionary-page pruning, VARIANT path pruning, BufferedParquetWriter, PFOR (experimental) and extended-precision timestamps (experimental). New in Core: MemoryBudget, one memory limit shared by concurrent scans; Azure and S3 uploads run in the background. Maturity: Parquet, Delta Lake, Expressions, Core and the cloud backends are the most mature; ORC and Avro are functional; Lance, Vortex and Iceberg are experimental. EngineeredWood is pre-1.0: every public API may change without notice or a deprecation cycle until 1.0.0. Pin an exact version.",
